From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 13:46:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(control): fall back to cascadia when libghostty will not
 start

PLAN lists this as a Phase 5 deliverable and two comments claimed it already
worked. It did not. GhosttyControlCore::Initialize returning false raises
RendererEnteredErrorState and TermControl gives up on the pane - the user is
told, and then left with a dead one. Nothing anywhere swapped in cascadia.

The fallback can only work before anything binds to the core, so it moves
into the engine factory: ControlInteractivity asks GhosttyEngine::TryGet()
first, and builds a cascadia core if the engine is not there. By the time
Initialize() can report a failure, TermControl has wired its events to the
core it was handed and there is nothing left to swap.

A surface that fails later still takes the Initialize/error-state route. That
failure is per-pane and the session may already have output in it; changing
engine underneath it would be worse than reporting.

GhosttyEngine gains _unavailableForTests, in the shape ControlCore already
uses for _inUnitTests: a machine where libghostty will not start is not a
state a test can reach by asking, and an untested fallback is one nobody has
seen work. Four tests in GhosttyEngineSelectionTests cover the factory, and
the fallback one is mutation-verified - removing the TryGet check fails it
and nothing else. The suite log also shows libghostty really does bootstrap
inside the TAEF host, so the ghostty branch is genuinely exercised rather
than always falling back.

unitControl 42/42, unitSettingsModel 159/159.
